+---
+type: adr
+status: stable
+entities: [Comment, CommentReport]
+related:
+  - app/Http/Controllers/CommentController.ts
+  - app/Http/Controllers/PostController.ts
+  - app/Http/Resources/CommentResource.ts
+  - app/Policies/CommentPolicy.ts
+generated: { by: "claude-fable/5.1", at: 2026-09-25T06:11:45.472Z }
+---
+
+# Community moderation hides reported comments
+
+## Context
+
+Readers can comment on posts, and there is no moderator on call. Comments
+must not become a spam channel one bad actor can fill.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Any signed-in user can report a comment. Reports are one row per
+  `(comment_id, user_id)` in `comment_reports`, unique, so a repeat report by
+  the same user changes nothing and the endpoint still answers 204.
+- A comment with reports from `COMMENT_HIDE_THRESHOLD` (3) or more distinct
+  users is left out of the post page's `comments` prop for everyone, including
+  its author and the post's author. The row stays in `comments` for review.
+- Deleting is a hard delete, allowed to the comment's author or the post's
+  author (`CommentPolicy.delete` receives both records).
+- Deleting a post deletes its comments and their reports explicitly in the
+  controller, because SQLite only honours `ON DELETE CASCADE` with the
+  `foreign_keys` pragma on, which the connection does not guarantee.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Hiding is computed per page render from the report count, so no denormalized
+counter can drift. A review screen can list hidden comments straight from the
+two tables; it is not part of this decision.
